{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794370051813,"sessionID":"ses_e37366a2affe5Df7hppu0PfBho","part":{"id":"prt_1c8ca1ecb001jD8AGNG0R9FNOD","messageID":"msg_1c8ca0fea001WlvY2XLIVCC2E4","sessionID":"ses_e37366a2affe5Df7hppu0PfBho","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794370051813,"sessionID":"ses_e37366a2affe5Df7hppu0PfBho","part":{"id":"prt_1c8ca1ecf0011idrINprxIYaG8","messageID":"msg_1c8ca0fea001WlvY2XLIVCC2E4","sessionID":"ses_e37366a2affe5Df7hppu0PfBho","type":"text","text":"<think>Good, pip install works with a proxy. Now let's check npm install for tailwindcss and react-router.\n\nLet me plan the architecture:\n\nBackend:\n- Flask app with SQLite at ./data/notes.db\n- Auth: register/login with token (use itsdangerous or simple random token stored in DB). Let's store tokens in a `sessions` table, or use itsdangerous signed tokens with a secret. Secret needs to persist across restart — store secret in data dir file.\n- Notes: id, title, content, tags, pinned, created_at, updated_at, author (username).\n- Endpoints as specified.\n\nFrontend:\n- React + TS + Vite + Tailwind. Need react-router for routing (note page). Let's check npm availability.\n\nLet me test npm install of tailwindcss v4 and react-router-dom.\n\nTailwind v4 with Vite uses @tailwindcss/vite plugin. Let's check versions available.\n\nLet me first check npm registry access.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794370051791,"end":1794370051809}}}
