{"type":"text","timestamp":1794370220402,"sessionID":"ses_e37366a2affe5Df7hppu0PfBho","part":{"id":"prt_1c8ccb164001lZawiyTwyQU9gZ","messageID":"msg_1c8cc9a2b001E1FPEaWFbk1n0m","sessionID":"ses_e37366a2affe5Df7hppu0PfBho","type":"text","text":"<think>The tags count was 0 because after setting tags to [] and deleting note 2 (which had the \"work\" tag), no tags remained. That's actually correct behavior — the tags endpoint lists \"every tag in use\". So the test assertion was wrong. Let me fix the test to keep a tag.\n\nActually wait — \"lists every tag in use with the number of notes carrying it\". Tags with zero notes shouldn't be listed since they're not \"in use\". My implementation deletes orphan tags anyway. Good.\n\nLet me update the test.</think>\n\nThe tag list was empty because the test cleared the last tag — expected behavior. Let me fix the test assertion.","time":{"start":1794370220388,"end":1794370220399}}}
