{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794370872237,"sessionID":"ses_e37366a2affe5Df7hppu0PfBho","part":{"id":"prt_1c8d6a399001Fxb1njG0tlmqEQ","messageID":"msg_1c8d68a4a001JPKCTpL5LIcxII","sessionID":"ses_e37366a2affe5Df7hppu0PfBho","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794370872237,"sessionID":"ses_e37366a2affe5Df7hppu0PfBho","part":{"id":"prt_1c8d6a39b001Fz36jlYiQbS2XO","messageID":"msg_1c8d68a4a001JPKCTpL5LIcxII","sessionID":"ses_e37366a2affe5Df7hppu0PfBho","type":"text","text":"<think>The server was killed when the shell command was terminated. The `pkill` in the compound command probably killed it, or the timeout killed the process group. Let me use a script approach with setsid and nohup properly detached. The issue: the shell tool terminates the command after timeout, which kills the process group.\n\nLet me write a start script and use `setsid` with full detachment.\n\nActually the issue earlier: `setsid nohup ... &` inside the same bash call that then gets killed at timeout — the whole process group gets killed. Let me start the server in a separate call with the command returning immediately.\n\nThe problem earlier was the command itself hung (the `&` with output redirect to a file should return). Hmm, the first attempt with `(... &)` returned output but the tool timed out because the background process kept stdout open? I redirected to server.log, so stdout shouldn't be held... but the tool waits for all descendants perhaps.\n\nLet me use `setsid` with full redirection and `</dev/null` and also disown. Let me try running it with `nohup ... & disown` and then `sleep 1; exit 0`.\n\nActually a simpler approach: use `at`-like daemonization via python's own double-fork. Or just start the server, run the tests, and kill it in a single command with a timeout.\n\nLet me do: start server in background, run tests, kill server - all in one command with `timeout`. That avoids the tool waiting.</think>\n\nThe background server gets killed when the shell command times out. Let me run the server and tests within a single command.","time":{"start":1794370872219,"end":1794370872233}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794370872260,"sessionID":"ses_e37366a2affe5Df7hppu0PfBho","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c8d69b4872928cea5130","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Starts the app, runs a command against it, then stops it.\nset -u\ncd /workspace\nPORT=\"${PORT:-8013}\"\nexport DATA_DIR=\"${DATA_DIR:-./data}\"\n\nsetsid nohup .venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0,'backend')\nimport app\napp.app.run(host='127.0.0.1', port=int('$PORT'))\n\" > /workspace/server.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &\nSERVER_PID=$!\n\nfor _ in $(seq 1 40); do\n  if curl -sf \"http://127.0.0.1:${PORT}/api/health\" > /dev/null; then break; fi\n  sleep 0.25\ndone\n\nBASE=\"http://127.0.0.1:${PORT}/api\" \"$@\"\nSTATUS=$?\n\nkill -TERM -\"$SERVER_PID\" 2>/dev/null\npkill -f \"port=int('$PORT')\" 2>/dev/null\nexit $STATUS\n","filePath":"/workspace/run_with_server.sh"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/run_with_server.sh","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"run_with_server.sh","time":{"start":1794370872230,"end":1794370872239}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8d6a39f001HbNI6ROKYCbryc","sessionID":"ses_e37366a2affe5Df7hppu0PfBho","messageID":"msg_1c8d68a4a001JPKCTpL5LIcxII"}}
